 "solver": {
  "description": "numpy re-implementation of the IsoME imaginary-axis equations (linearized at Tc): cdos = constant DOS with a fixed Morel-Anderson mu* applied up to the Matsubara cutoff omega_c; vdos = full-bandwidth equations with the energy-dependent DOS N(e), the energy shift chi and a self-consistent chemical potential, fixed mu*; vdos_W = the same with the archived static W(e,e') in place of mu* (phi = phi_ph(i w_n) + phi_c(e)).",
  "conventions": "alpha2F from the solver_column listed in each inputs result (the column used by the archived IsoME runs); DOS from the inputs DOS file divided by 2 for spin; energy grid 1/5/50 meV inside +-100/+-500/+-5000 meV of E_F; default omega_c = 7000 meV (allowed 300-7000); Tc to 0.01 K, search range 10-500 K.",
  "validation": "Where archived IsoME runs exist, the lab reproduces their Tc (fixed mu* and full W) to within 2 %."
 },
